Nitrogen
Nutrient_ID: N001
Nutrient_Name: Nitrogen
Nutrient_Type: Primary macronutrient
Main_Function: Promotes vegetative growth and chlorophyll formation
Deficiency_Symptoms: Yellowing of older leaves and stunted growth
Common_Sources: Urea Ammonium Sulphate Farmyard Manure
Management: Apply in split doses to reduce leaching loss

Phosphorus
Nutrient_ID: N002
Nutrient_Name: Phosphorus
Nutrient_Type: Primary macronutrient
Main_Function: Promotes root development and flowering
Deficiency_Symptoms: Purplish discoloration of leaves and poor root growth
Common_Sources: Diammonium Phosphate Single Super Phosphate
Management: Apply as basal dose close to root zone

Potassium
Nutrient_ID: N003
Nutrient_Name: Potassium
Nutrient_Type: Primary macronutrient
Main_Function: Improves quality and stress tolerance
Deficiency_Symptoms: Yellowing and scorching of leaf margins
Common_Sources: Muriate of Potash Sulphate of Potash
Management: Apply based on soil test and crop stage requirement

Calcium
Nutrient_ID: N004
Nutrient_Name: Calcium
Nutrient_Type: Secondary macronutrient
Main_Function: Cell wall development and fruit quality
Deficiency_Symptoms: Blossom end rot in fruits and distorted new growth
Common_Sources: Gypsum Lime Farmyard Manure
Management: Apply as soil amendment or foliar spray as needed

Magnesium
